 ('frz7', 'And women. In the early Vedic period women took part in rituals and in debate, and the texts name some of them: Gargi, who questions a teacher closely in the Upanishads; Maitreyi, who asks what wealth is worth if it does not bring immortality; Lopamudra, to whom hymns are attributed.'),
